{
  "about": "Shared by packages/exactdocs/tests/ingestion/test_chunker.py and web/src/features/browse/render/anchors.test.ts. `anchors` are the anchors of the top-level headings, in order; the chunker and the web renderer must agree on every one.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "plain words",
      "markdown": "# Getting Started\n\n## Install it\n",
      "anchors": [
        "getting-started",
        "install-it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "punctuation drops, dashes and underscores stay",
      "markdown": "# What's new? (v2.0)\n\n## snake_case - and -dashes\n",
      "anchors": [
        "whats-new-v20",
        "snake_case---and--dashes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "markup is plain text, code keeps its text",
      "markdown": "# The `fetch()` *option* and [a link](http://x.test)\n",
      "anchors": [
        "the-fetch-option-and-a-link"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "repeats count across the whole article, at every level",
      "markdown": "# Usage\n\n## Usage\n\n### Usage\n\n## Usage 1\n\n## Usage\n",
      "anchors": [
        "usage",
        "usage-1",
        "usage-2",
        "usage-1-1",
        "usage-3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a taken suffix is skipped, and an issued slug is remembered",
      "markdown": "# A\n\n# A 1\n\n# A\n\n# A\n",
      "anchors": [
        "a",
        "a-1",
        "a-2",
        "a-3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "headings in block quotes take a slug but are not chunks",
      "markdown": "> # Same\n\n# Same\n",
      "anchors": [
        "same-1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "inline HTML tags add no text, their content does",
      "markdown": "# Hello <b>bold</b> world\n\n# <span>only</span>\n",
      "anchors": [
        "hello-bold-world",
        "only"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "images contribute their alt text",
      "markdown": "# ![the logo](a.png) Logo\n",
      "anchors": [
        "the-logo-logo"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "unicode letters and digits stay, symbols and emoji go",
      "markdown": "# Zażółć gęślą jaźń\n\n# Привет, мир\n\n# 日本語の見出し\n\n# Rocket 🚀 launch ②\n\n# İstanbul ΣΑΣ Straße\n",
      "anchors": [
        "zażółć-gęślą-jaźń",
        "привет-мир",
        "日本語の見出し",
        "rocket--launch-②",
        "istanbul-σας-straße"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "setext headings, trailing hashes and extra spaces",
      "markdown": "Title\n=====\n\nSub  title\n---------\n\n## Closed ##\n",
      "anchors": [
        "title",
        "sub--title",
        "closed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a heading made of symbols only has an empty slug",
      "markdown": "# ???\n\n# !!!\n",
      "anchors": [
        "",
        "-1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "fenced code is not a heading",
      "markdown": "# Real\n\n```md\n# Real\n```\n\n# Real\n",
      "anchors": [
        "real",
        "real-1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "escapes and entities are not text",
      "markdown": "# snake\\_case &amp; a\\*b\n\n# Tom &amp; Jerry\n",
      "anchors": [
        "snake_case--ab",
        "tom--jerry"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "an attribute list sets the anchor (MkDocs attr_list)",
      "markdown": "# Async Tests { #async-tests }\n\n## HTTPX { #httpx }\n",
      "anchors": [
        "async-tests",
        "httpx"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "an id without spaces (Docusaurus)",
      "markdown": "## Hello World {#my-explicit-id}\n",
      "anchors": [
        "my-explicit-id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "an id among classes and keys, with or without the colon",
      "markdown": "## Usage {: #use .wide data-x=\"a b\" }\n\n## Setup { .note #setup lang=en }\n",
      "anchors": [
        "use",
        "setup"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "classes only: the text without them is slugged",
      "markdown": "## Options { .note }\n",
      "anchors": [
        "options"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "braces that are not a trailing attribute list stay",
      "markdown": "## The `{#x}` literal\n\n## Use `{#y}`\n\n## A set {1, 2}\n\n## Empty {}\n\n## Word { x }\n",
      "anchors": [
        "the-x-literal",
        "use-y",
        "a-set-1-2",
        "empty-",
        "word--x-"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "an explicit id is taken like a slug",
      "markdown": "## A {#a}\n\n## A\n",
      "anchors": [
        "a",
        "a-1"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
